{%- comment -%}
  casa-breadcrumb-collection.liquid
  Used by: blocks/breadcrumbs.liquid (live visible crumb),
           snippets/casa-jsonld-breadcrumbs.liquid (structured data),
           blocks/casa-title.liquid, blocks/casa-breadcrumbs.liquid,
           snippets/breadcrumbs.liquid (legacy).

  Echoes the HANDLE of the collection that should be the middle breadcrumb
  crumb for a product — or "" when none is suitable. Every breadcrumb renderer
  goes through this one snippet so the visible crumb and the JSON-LD can never
  disagree.

  Pass the product explicitly from block scope:
    {%- render 'casa-breadcrumb-collection', product: closest.product -%}
  In <head>/section scope the global `product` is used automatically.

  Selection order:
    1. Merchant-set primary — the per-product metafield
       `custom.casa_breadcrumb_value` (Collection reference). Explicit merchant
       choice, always wins. (Wrong crumb here = fix the metafield in Admin.)
    2. Fallback — the product's first REAL CATEGORY collection, chosen from the
       casa_bc_categories ALLOW-list below, in that priority order.
    3. Otherwise "" → breadcrumb shows Home / Product only.

  Why an allow-list, not a block-list: a block-list of "junk" collections fails
  WRONG — any new marketing/ops collection a merchant creates (a "6 Must-Have's",
  "Trending", "Back to School", "Father's Day Gifts"…) silently becomes a
  breadcrumb until someone adds it to the list. The allow-list fails SAFE: only
  genuine product categories can ever be a crumb; anything unknown is skipped and
  the crumb is omitted rather than showing junk. When you add a NEW product
  category collection, add its handle here (most specific first).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign casa_bc_categories = 'cleansers,toners-1,essences,serums-1,treatments-1,exfoliators,masks,eye-cream,moisturizers,sunscreens-1,makeup,wellness-rituals' | split: ','

  assign casa_bc_chosen = ''

  # 1. Merchant-set primary collection (per-product metafield) — explicit choice wins.
  assign casa_bc_meta = product.metafields.custom.casa_breadcrumb_value.value
  if casa_bc_meta != blank and casa_bc_meta.handle != blank
    assign casa_bc_chosen = casa_bc_meta.handle
  endif

  # 2. Fallback: first real category the product belongs to, in allow-list priority.
  if casa_bc_chosen == '' and product != blank
    assign casa_bc_product_handles = product.collections | map: 'handle'
    for casa_bc_cat in casa_bc_categories
      if casa_bc_product_handles contains casa_bc_cat
        assign casa_bc_chosen = casa_bc_cat
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  echo casa_bc_chosen
-%}
